{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars","id":1420855,"title":"Ideas for Avatars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-29T12:41:07-07:00","id":1420855,"title":"Ideas for Avatars","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> thank you for reading this.<br /> I'm new to storytelling Mage(20). I have experience with Vampire, but Mage is a new challenge for me.<br /> <br /> I've got some hard time thinking about a suitable Avatar for one of my player characters. My players only gave me some very vague hints for their Avatars, but for most I got an idea, but not this one.<br /> The character is an Akashic, but without strong ties to the traditions or wisdom of his Tradition, as far as he has been played since the game started not long ago. The Character has an avatars background of 5 and a primordial essence. The only input from my player was, that the Avatar shows itself in the form of an eastern dragon and the character thinks of the Avatar as a manifestation of his own chi.<br /> Now I'm thinking about this Avatar. I can't find a good agenda or goals for the Avatar or what cosmic principle the Avatar might be tied to. I want to bring the Avatars of my PCs more into the game, but I can't come up with good ideas for this one. Maybe someone here can help me with ideas for the Avatar?<br /> <br /> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T13:25:53-07:00","id":1420861,"title":"","content":"You're pretty spoiled for choice when it comes to existing mythological dragons you could pick from rather than creating one yourself.<br /> <br /> I'd start with what specific culture(s) the character connects to, both in terms of ethnicity and philosophy/religion to start to narrow things down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T14:19:12-07:00","id":1420870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars#post1420855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone,<br /> thank you for reading this.<br /> I'm new to storytelling Mage(20). I have experience with Vampire, but Mage is a new challenge for me.<br /> <br /> I've got some hard time thinking about a suitable Avatar for one of my player characters. My players only gave me some very vague hints for their Avatars, but for most I got an idea, but not this one.<br /> The character is an Akashic, but without strong ties to the traditions or wisdom of his Tradition, as far as he has been played since the game started not long ago. The Character has an avatars background of 5 and a primordial essence. The only input from my player was, that the Avatar shows itself in the form of an eastern dragon and the character thinks of the Avatar as a manifestation of his own chi.<br /> Now I'm thinking about this Avatar. I can't find a good agenda or goals for the Avatar or what cosmic principle the Avatar might be tied to. I want to bring the Avatars of my PCs more into the game, but I can't come up with good ideas for this one. Maybe someone here can help me with ideas for the Avatar?<br /> <br /> Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Use Chinese Astrology. It is based on a system of twelve animals, of which the dragon is the only necessarily-mythical one, and elements (wood, fire, earth, metal, water). It is a 60 year cycle. The Dragon has well defined personality characteristics and the combination of elements can further define the avatar's personality. The player does not have to be born on a year that corresponds to the dragon. Mage allows past lives as part of a backstory and I would not require taking a past lives background, especially if the player has already allocated their background and freebie points. Just make the avatar having been waiting for the player to physically incarnate since the time it came into the world.<br /> <br /> Another useful exercise is to imagine - totally hypothetically - what would happen if the player was conscripted into the New World Order or voluntarily defected. Leaving the Akashic brotherhood would not cut the player off from their avatar. Being inside the technocracy would provide different opportunities to pursue the worldly agenda of the avatar. I know Technocracy Reloaded will have something about the five elemental dragons. Avatar exists in a context independent from Tradition, even if it currently lines up perfectly with the paradigm and focal practice offered by the MENTOR.<br /> <br /> In games with a lot of players, you want to economize on NPC characters. If you had four players and each has a Mentor and Avatar, you are looking at eight NPCs to create, in addition to the NPCs necessary to the plot conflict. I don't do this to spare my sanity. It can be assumed that they have concluded the training that their mentor had to offer.<br /> <br /> Characteristics I believe Dragon has:<br /> - Perceived as lazy because he conserves his energy for times of crisis. While everyone else is dealing with day to day problems, the dragon sits back and analyzes the situation, trying to determine when the right to act is.<br /> - When the trouble threatens to overwhelm his circle of friends, he &quot;breathes fire&quot;, uses up the conserved energy.<br /> - He suffers from vanity.<br /> - He does what is impossible, because he doesn't know it is impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_(zodiac)#Years_and_the_Five_Elements\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Chinese_black_dragon.svg/1280px-Chinese_black_dragon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_(zodiac)#Years_and_the_Five_Elements\" target=\"_blank\"> Dragon (zodiac) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_(zodiac)#Years_and_the_Five_Elements\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_(zodiac)#Years_and_the_Five_Elements </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T14:46:56-07:00","id":1420874,"title":"","content":"I would say a vain metal dragon, it's scales are so polished all it does is stare at it's own reflection until it finally has to do something....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 10-29-2020, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T22:11:12-07:00","id":1420936,"title":"","content":"I've been designing some pregenerated characters for my upcoming Mage chronicle, and one of them has an eastern dragon motif. His avatar is the &quot;soul of a dragon,&quot; but he also has a Mentor/Ally that <i>is</i> a dragon, and he doesn't really understand the difference between his avatar and his mentor, since both appear to him as a dragon in dreams and visions -- and also because his avatar and the dragon are aligned in purpose and intent. Both desire to see a return to the Golden Age of Magic, and that's their agenda -- to mold the mage into a warrior in the Ascension War who can help tip the balance in favor of dragons, allowing them to return to the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26385-gailbraithe","name":"Gailbraithe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26385_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T23:06:28-07:00","id":1420941,"title":"","content":"If you wish, you <i>could</i> make them one and the same. Taking the Manifest Avatar Merit gives the Avatar its own character traits (<b>Book of Secrets</b> p.71); taking it as an Ally as well gives it a physical presence of its own (same reference). By default, a Manifest Avatar only manifests when it wants to; if you want it to be permanently manifested, you can also take the Phylactery Flaw (<b>Book of Secrets</b> pp.94\u201396).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T18:27:30-07:00","id":1421079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars#post1420855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm thinking about this Avatar. I can't find a good agenda or goals for the Avatar or what cosmic principle the Avatar might be tied to. I want to bring the Avatars of my PCs more into the game, but I can't come up with good ideas for this one. Maybe someone here can help me with ideas for the Avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordial. <br /> Eastern/Asian Dragon.<br /> Avatar rating of 5.<br /> No strong ties to &quot;traditional&quot; Akashic styles/tropes.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> His Avatar is Godzilla. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T17:31:05-07:00","id":1421236,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thank you for your input. I've read about the Chinese zodiac Dragon personality traits. That is a good start. The idea to think of Godzilla is good, too. The character serves the trope &quot;a cop who knows kung fu&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Regarding the agendas of the various Avatars, I'm thinking about giving all avatars a connecting goal/interest to keep the characters together, because their personalities are very different (and I want more reason for the characters to stay together than being the PCs).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Son of Ether, pattern Avatar: Avatar wants to work against the corruption of the world, so he wants his mage to invent things to prevent that (like filters that help against pollution)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Verbena, questing Avatar: Avatar wants to restore healthy nature, therefore he wants his mage to fight pollution and the corruption that strengthens these forces.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Celestrial Chorister, pattern or dynamic Avatar (the player did not decide yet): His Avatar wants to defend the world against the corruption, so he wants his mage to fight those forces in each way possible for him.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Akashic Brother, primordial Avatar (the aforementioned): His Avatar wants him to rid the Akashic Brotherhood from corrupting influences and hunt down fallen Brothers.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Virtual Adept, questing Avatar: Avatar wants to end Ascension war between Traditions and Technocracy so they can join forces against corruption, so he wants his mage to be diplomatic and compassionate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What do you think?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thanks for your posts.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T19:18:27-07:00","id":1421252,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want the Virtual Adept to step up to the plate and find common ground with the Technocracy, what about them realizing that the Nephandi have won the battle for Information Technology? That's pretty much following M20 Book of the Fallen and the Technocracy Reloaded package so far--humans got the Internet and are using it to act in their worst possible ways more often than in good ways. The Internet fosters so many hate groups.<br /> <br /> For the Akashic Brotherhood character, well as the people who hold the Seat of Mind on the Traditions Council, where were they protecting the minds of Sleepers? Despite the rise of martial arts in cinema and more and more martial arts being televised and the rise in yoga, how much of that is teaching the fundamental teachings of those paradigms for human improvement and how much of that has been taken over by people who don't know the cultures behind it and want to extinguish those cultures or monetize them? If the Akashic Brotherhood is a kung fu cop, they could certainly be working to prevent corruption within the Akashic Brotherhood. I'd also add complacency in teaching the ideals as an enemy of the Akashic Brotherhood--while the ancient ways may not be perfect they have value and this is not being taught as societies change.<br /> <br /> Godzilla in the first movie is a reminder about the perils of science--the atomic bomb gives him power and he's there to protect the environment. Hence, Godzilla could have reason to work with the Verbena and Sons of Ether. See, although the Technocracy are far from perfect, their general goal is to make the world a better place for humanity. However, technology has been corrupted by the Technephandi (again lots on them in M20 Book of the Fallen and you can pretty much raid Werewolf for Pentex and any nasty groups in Vampire that you want to be evil mad scientists) and even parts of the Technocracy are rotten.<br /> <br /> So much of what makes a Chronicle fun is getting to run a story that you and the players enjoy. I hope you find such. . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T00:39:30-08:00","id":1421399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421252#post1421252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you want the Virtual Adept to step up to the plate and find common ground with the Technocracy, what about them realizing that the Nephandi have won the battle for Information Technology? That's pretty much following M20 Book of the Fallen and the Technocracy Reloaded package so far--humans got the Internet and are using it to act in their worst possible ways more often than in good ways. The Internet fosters so many hate groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Book Of The Fallen advisable to use as head-canon? Considering...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars#post1420855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new to storytelling Mage(20). I have experience with Vampire, but Mage is a new challenge for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three important points to make about Book Of The Fallen:<br /> 1. The author based the writing on having experienced a lot of second hand horror, mostly involving being powerless to extricate someone you care about from ongoing abuse. One can acquire PTSD, merely knowing about or witnessing someone else's experience. The writing is informed by familiarity with real world evil (if we characterize abusers as evil, which intervening mental health professionals do not).<br /> 2. It then goes on to explain how Nephandi NPCs, based on bad people in the world, would organize to erode their victims' agency, resistance and moral convictions. If you want to convincingly roleplay reprehensibly mean NPCs, very effectively, BOTF will give you that.<br /> 3 It has warnings and guidelines on how to do this safely. Cpt7, P212, &quot;Storyteller Responsibilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> Assuming some of Caliginosa's players are new to roleplaying, this might - has a slight chance to - go wrong, in one of two ways.<br /> <br /> 1. So restricting yourself from playing the villain that you can't do it convincingly. They are easy to kill, because your don't use the most cunning strategy available to them.<br /> 2. Methodically following the &quot;guide to evil tactics&quot; and doing it too well, leaving at least one player uneasy about the game, on reflection.<br /> <br /> To take an example of something at the opposite end of the scale, in which a character deals with demonic forces, Planescape: Torment, The Brothel for Slaking Intellectual Lusts. A guy who can't die must resolve the personal dilemmas of escorts working for a sexy fiend. It is incredibly light hearted.<br /> <br /> Somewhere between BOTF and Torment is each player's fun-zone. I would say, mine BOTF for Nephandi factions and Acolyte groups, but disregard the &quot;true evil 101: tactics manual&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421236#post1421236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Regarding the agendas of the various Avatars, I'm thinking about giving all avatars a connecting goal/interest to keep the characters together, because their personalities are very different (and I want more reason for the characters to stay together than being the PCs).</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's good storytelling, particularly with sizeable a group. For a group of five or six, cohesion is essential. That being said, let's look at the Avatar combos. <br /> <br /> I'm just going to reorder the list so the two questing avatars can be compared first. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421236#post1421236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Verbena, questing Avatar: Avatar wants to restore healthy nature, therefore he wants his mage to fight pollution and the corruption that strengthens these forces.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421236#post1421236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Virtual Adept, questing Avatar: Avatar wants to end Ascension war between Traditions and Technocracy so they can join forces against corruption, so he wants his mage to be diplomatic and compassionate.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The completion of a Seeking for these two is not the achievement of the goal, but a point where their effort transforms them personally for the better.<br /> <br /> Verbena - restore nature, fight pollution, fight corruption (assuming corporate lobbying, Appointment of Global Warming Denialists to run government agencies dealing with human health and environmental issues, which the cronies then neuter)<br /> <br /> VA - end the Ascension War, fight the Wyrm united. <br /> Use diplomacy. <br /> This means making promises. You should make his life complicated, having multiple obligations to conflicting parties. A VR meeting could be a way to allow enemies who would kill each other, if they met in person, to talk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421236#post1421236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Son of Ether, pattern Avatar: Avatar wants to work against the corruption of the world, so he wants his mage to invent things to prevent that (like filters that help against pollution)</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">High Matter and Forces could allow graphene to be made in quantities greater than is currently possible. Graphene can be stretched to allow some molecules through, holding larger ones back. It is usable for desalinization. You can also make loose fitting bulletproof clothes from it.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421236#post1421236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Celestrial Chorister, pattern or dynamic Avatar (the player did not decide yet): His Avatar wants to defend the world against the corruption, so he wants his mage to fight those forces in each way possible for him.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis might be a source of inspiration. Be ready to see something.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G6v48-w9sTA&amp;ab_channel=corpuscollossus\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G6v48-w9sTA&amp;ab_channel=corpuscollossus\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G6v48-w9sTA&amp;ab_channel=corpuscollossus\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G6v48-w9sTA&amp;ab_channel=corpuscollossus </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421236#post1421236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Akashic Brother, primordial Avatar (the aforementioned): His Avatar wants him to rid the Akashic Brotherhood from corrupting influences and hunt down fallen Brothers.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>With Mind, he and some other Akashics could establish a telepathic information network that collects and shares information about AB-Barrabi. He makes their lives so miserable that they have to come after him - total Dragon style. <br /> <br /> If the Avatars' goals are intertwined, do the same for a group of enemy NPCs. Killing one makes the others stronger. They are never all in one place. Corr4, Life4, Prime3, Mind4, Spirit5 effect. How do you counteract such a group? Can the players begin to acquire such power? <br /> <br /> With five players all reading your social cues, the secret affiliation one of your NPCs has to the Nephandi that you were planning to conceal until later might become obvious to them. Here are some steps you can take to keep players guessing and debating their options. <br /> <br /> 1. Create the Mage NPCs as they would be without having been tricked into the Caul. Make them so that they have clear agendas, unrelated to potential nephandic corruption. Decide the ratio. The chances of correctly guessing which three Technomancers out of ten are Nephandi is very low. It's easy to make the Syndicate - Disbursements Mage a Wyrm-Barrabi. Players will guess that one quick. Instead, find reasons that appeal to the personal weakness of each NPC that explain their fall. One could be an environmental crusader who lost a private one on one debate with convincing Wyrm servitor. They carry on playing eco-warrior while using their activist network for evil ends. Have at least one who is either an Infernalist or a K'llashaa, not particularly dedicated to spreading pollution, which Malfeans (Wyrm-servants) often want to do. <br /> <br /> 2. Make the spread of corruption something happening in real time. Imagine one Nephandi inside the Technocratic Union making careful plans to sidle up to a college at a time of weakness and pulling them in slow steps toward the fall. Have the target who doesn't know the corrupter's true allegiance do things that morally damn them. Have the Traditions suffer deep losses as a result. If your players pursue justice, they may forgo the chance at peace and to save this NPC.<br /> <br /> 3. Create NPCs, Mage or Sleeper, involved in extractive industries, who believe they are doing good by supplying what people &quot;need&quot;. Narratively explain a corporate culture that downplays environmental impact and touts the benefits to society of the business activity. <br /> <br /> 4. Create a non-nephandi Mage NPC or group with a Malthusian Agenda. If overpopulation is a driver of pollution, imagine solutions that are indifferent to human life. Force the payers to work with someone from examples #2 and #3 to stop the plan. <br /> <br /> 5. Multinational corporations and billionaires don't have their wealth stored in the countries where it is made. In addition to tourism, island economies often have a banking sector that serves tax evaders and drug cartels. Steal from the rich? What about the threat of sea level rise to these islands? <br /> <br /> 6. If some of the players are innovators or green capitalists, force them to decide between empire building and stopping a threat (like a planned clearcutting of a forest or jungle). If they fail to stop the clearcutting, the trees are gone. If they use all their energy to stop the latest threat, they never define themselves by what they can build. <br /> <br /> 7. Before adding Wyrm Blights to your map, think about pollution in a chemical sense. Is there a microbe that can turn a polluting chemical into something beneficial to nature? The Etherite would be interested in this. <br /> <br /> 8. Bribery is legal. Often the relationship between bent politicians and rapacious industries are known to the public. Well funded attack ads against the other candidate sway voters nearly every time. <br /> <br /> 9. Create a conflict unrelated to corporate greed or pollution that complicates the landscape. Territorial gang wars in a neighborhood. Some mutant monsters escaped from a Progenitor lab and now stalk a valley. People want answers to the disappearances. <br /> <br /> 10. Make Technocracy Nodes and Constructs powerful, opaque (resistant to scrying) and foreboding. Build a maze, if you have the time. <br /> <br /> If you haven't already seen the movie, &quot;The East&quot;, I would watch it.<br /> Check out &quot;Represent Us&quot; YouTube channel. <br /> <br /> btw, do you use M20 session-xp criteria? How much xp do you give per session?<br /> <br /> How did the most recent session go? I hope you are having fun storytelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T11:45:56-08:00","id":1421487,"title":"","content":"Book of the Fallen is an official M20 book. A lot of work went into it and unlike prior takes on the Nephandi, it's got a great deal of depth and nuance. It's also one of those books where the warning label is no lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T15:57:38-08:00","id":1421515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421487#post1421487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of the Fallen is an official M20 book. A lot of work went into it and unlike prior takes on the Nephandi, it's got a great deal of depth and nuance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Official M20 - yes. A lot of work, well written - agreed. I said that it is informed by the author's experience. To be more specific, One of the Authors, since it is co-authored by Satyros Phil Brucato and Jacqueline Bryk. I was referring to the Author's preface in the #1 part of my comment. If it were a preface written by both authors, it would be, &quot;Authors' Preface&quot;. The apostrophe comes before the s. The preface is written by one of the authors, not specified. I assume it was Satyros, whose name appears fist in credits.<br /> <br /> Your recommending the resource to Caliginosa - good. I included my thoughts on using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421399#post1421399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say, mine BOTF for Nephandi factions and Acolyte groups, but disregard the &quot;true evil 101: tactics manual&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question on whether this is advisable to use BOTF as head-canon isn't pointed at you. It is based on a couple of impressions I took from Caliginosa's description of his campaign. &quot;The Corruption&quot;, is a term used throughout the outline of the chronicle's vision along side &quot;pollution&quot;. It is an exploration of those issues, through creative roleplay. There is a lot that can be said about mundane political corruption, against public interest and human survivability, in favor of short term corporate interests. The Nephandi, as previously represented, are a useful character-representation for this form of corruption.<br /> <br /> If the storyteller is bringing four players together to brainstorm solutions to problems on everyone's mind through creative play, they are probably best to roll forward with that. The campaign is not described as, for example, being centered on intervention into cycles of abuse. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421487#post1421487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also one of those books where the warning label is no lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this label is to be taken seriously, before the campaign starts, there has to be a sit-down discussion. &quot;Okay guys. We need to talk about techniques used by abusers and how to resist, because my NPCs are going to be members of organized bullying networks, so you need to be prepared.&quot;. The focus is taken off of the intended theme of Unified Intervention Into Political Corruption Impacting the Environment.<br /> <br /> The Internet or the Digital Web being Nephandi territory isn't conducive to this kind of campaign, if that is how we are interpreting BOTF. The real situation on which the chronicle is based is bleak enough. In reality, the Internet is a place where organization against Corporate Ecocide has a good chance of succeeding. <br /> <br /> Also, I would say that BOTF's description of the culture of Silicon Valley has become somewhat outdated in the short time since it's release. However, I would not wish to use Caliginosa's post as the place to discuss this. It may be some time before I would be prepared to make an original post about BOTF and adequately address replies. I still have not gotten back to contributors to my Population Growth in Mystic Paradigm Parallel World post. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420855-ideas-for-avatars?p=1421252#post1421252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much of what makes a Chronicle fun is getting to run a story that you and the players enjoy. I hope you find such. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Have fun. I hope your chronicle leads to more great ideas. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T16:19:58-08:00","id":1421519,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> <br /> usually I give an average of 2 XP per session and between 6 and 8 at the end of a story. At the moment the PCs have 89 XP total. The group decided together on the average amount of XP.<br /> <br /> Storytelling is a lot of fun, but since we're in a lockdown again, we're playing online and I think it's much more exhausting than meeting in person. When two people start taking at the same time, you have no chance to understand anyone, so things have to be repeated.<br /> I prefer storytelli g and even when running another game (like Shadowrun) I'm more into storytelling than &quot;classical&quot; game mastering, I think. <br /> <br /> The last session I ran was good, I had my group in a conflict about a ghost who wanted revenge to be free (destroy his last getter to resolve his last thing that kept him from going on, but that was a person). The group had the control about the access of the ghost to that person. The conflict was regarded as something very good by the players. <br /> <br /> The group had one encounter with a Nephandus (Etherite barabbi) who poisoned a swamp 50 years ago, but he simply left and the Verbena decided that he was his arch enemy from now on. Though they cannot reach that one at the moment. No more about corruption yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T12:56:43-08:00","id":1422645,"title":"","content":"I've allowed some of the DTF concepts shape my thinking about avatars. There were hints about God becoming 'fragmented' trying to save the world, which fits in with some of the ideas of the One and all and being fragments of the divine (IIRC those correctly) I also interptred 'days of fire' as suggesting that perhaps some mages came from the remnants of eradicated rebel/loyalist angels (there have been parallels between Lores and True Magick in DtF too) - if anything I tend to view it as an indication that approaches to magic may have been massively more diverse than the game system lets on in the past (towards 'modern' times by and large it would consolidate to the sphere system which in many ways is the penultimate approach to MtA magic.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}